# PULSAR — the HERMETIC coverage gate (audit M-15, 2026-10-22).
#
# The problem this file exists to solve:
#
#   The old gate measured one number over "whatever could run in this
#   environment". With the Firestore emulator up, the integration tests run and
#   the figure is ~79%; without it they skip and the figure is ~74%. Same code,
#   same tests — a different number, and a floor of 79 that is only reachable on
#   a machine that happens to have an emulator started. A ratchet that depends on
#   the environment is not a ratchet; it is a coin flip that fails builds.
#
# The fix is a SPLIT, not a lower floor:
#
#   1. THIS gate is hermetic. It runs `pytest -m "not emulator and not chain"`
#      with FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST explicitly unset, so no test can silently
#      become runnable or unrunnable. It must pass on every machine, in CI, and
#      on a laptop with no network.
#   2. The complete gate (.coveragerc, floor 79) still exists for the
#      emulator+anvil configuration, and reports the higher number. It is
#      reported as a SEPARATE gate whose name says it needs those services.
#
# Measured, not guessed: 74% / 3937 statements / 1011 missed, identical across
# consecutive runs (two runs on 2026-10-22 produced byte-identical totals).
#
# Raise `fail_under` only in the commit that adds the tests.
[run]
source = api
data_file = .coverage.hermetic
omit =
    api/requirements*.txt

[report]
fail_under = 74
show_missing = True
skip_covered = False
exclude_lines =
    pragma: no cover
    if TYPE_CHECKING:
    raise NotImplementedError
    \.\.\.
